thread.content:
Splitting out the remaining phases as the execution agent recommended, with the existing in-review item kept as the seam-only deliverable.

```json
{
  "form": "mutation_list",
  "rationale": "Execution agent shipped only Phases 1–2 (seam) of the auto-apply-defaults plan; split remaining phases (3a, 3b, GC, schema-version coordination, follow-ups) into separate items so each can land reviewably, and re-point downstream dependencies to the load-bearing Phase 3b item.",
  "mutations": [
    {
      "id": "m1",
      "op": "update_item",
      "target": "execute/agent-manager-sandbox-auto-apply-defaults",
      "patch": {
        "title": "Land workspace-sandbox apply-at-run-end seam (Phases 1–2 of auto-apply-defaults)",
        "description": "Scope reduced to what actually shipped: domain types, the new `POST /api/v1/sandboxes/{id}/apply-at-run-end` endpoint, validation, audit annotations, schema-version-ready provenance fields, and unit tests. Legacy `tryAutoApproval` / `AutoApprove` / `AutoReject` / `DisableAutoApproveIfEmpty` / `RequiresApproval` fields remain in place as deprecated. Run-executor wiring, GC, schema-version package, and the headline run-executor tests are tracked as separate items (Phase 3a, Phase 3b, Phase 4, Phase 5). Do not merge operator-visible behavior on this item alone — it is forward-compatible but observable only once Phase 3b lands."
      },
      "rationale": "Feedback: agent only completed Phases 1–2; the in-review item should reflect that narrower scope so reviewers don't expect end-to-end behavior."
    },
    {
      "id": "m2",
      "op": "add_item",
      "item": {
        "kind": "execute",
        "name": "agent-manager-apply-at-run-end-provider-seam",
        "title": "Add Provider.ApplyAtRunEnd seam on agent-manager + workspace_sandbox adapter (Phase 3a)",
        "description": "Add `Provider.ApplyAtRunEnd` to the agent-manager sandbox provider seam, implement it in the `workspace_sandbox.go` adapter against the new `POST /api/v1/sandboxes/{id}/apply-at-run-end` endpoint, and cover the wire call with adapter tests. No run-executor behavior change yet — this is the wire-level prerequisite for Phase 3b. Locked contract reference: `scenarios/swarm-manager/research/agent-sandbox-auditability-contract`.",
        "priority": 1,
        "effort": "M",
        "depends_on": ["execute/agent-manager-sandbox-auto-apply-defaults"]
      },
      "rationale": "Execution agent recommended landing Phase 3 in two sub-cuts; 3a is the reviewable wire-level prerequisite with no behavior flip."
    },
    {
      "id": "m3",
      "op": "add_item",
      "item": {
        "kind": "execute",
        "name": "agent-manager-run-executor-apply-at-run-end-cutover",
        "title": "Cut run executor over to applyAtRunEnd and remove legacy auto-approval fields (Phase 3b)",
        "description": "Replace `tryAutoApproval` with a single shared `applyAtRunEnd` call site after the terminal handlers in `Execute()`. Add the eager provenance write at sandbox setup, wire `RunOutcome.ToContract` (7→4 mapping), remove the deprecated legacy fields (`SandboxAcceptanceConfig.AutoApprove` / `AutoReject` / `DisableAutoApproveIfEmpty`, `RunConfig.RequiresApproval`), update proto + generated code, fix `orchestration/sandbox_config_test.go` fixtures, and write the six plan-specified run-executor test cases (success-apply, failure-apply, partial-acceptance split, manualReview-deferred, no-op empty-provenance, ConversationID inheritance). This is the load-bearing cut that flips behavior end-to-end. Locked contract reference: `scenarios/swarm-manager/research/agent-sandbox-auditability-contract`.",
        "priority": 1,
        "effort": "L",
        "depends_on": ["execute/agent-manager-apply-at-run-end-provider-seam"]
      },
      "rationale": "Phase 3b is the behavior-flipping cut; isolating it keeps the diff reviewable and gives a single clear merge gate for downstream rollout/e2e items."
    },
    {
      "id": "m4",
      "op": "add_item",
      "item": {
        "kind": "execute",
        "name": "workspace-sandbox-manual-review-ttl-gc",
        "title": "Implement manualReview TTL GC in LifecycleReconciler (Phase 4)",
        "description": "Wire `ManualReviewTTL` (already present on `LifecycleConfig`, env var `WORKSPACE_SANDBOX_MANUAL_REVIEW_TTL`) into `LifecycleReconciler.ReconcileLifecycle` so abandoned `manualReview=true` sandboxes are auto-denied on TTL expiry instead of leaking indefinitely. Clock-injected TTL expiry test required. Self-contained; can land in parallel with or after Phase 3.",
        "priority": 2,
        "effort": "S",
        "depends_on": ["execute/agent-manager-sandbox-auto-apply-defaults"]
      },
      "rationale": "Plan's Phase 4 is unimplemented; the config knob exists but nothing reads it. Splitting it out lets it land in parallel with Phase 3."
    },
    {
      "id": "m5",
      "op": "add_item",
      "item": {
        "kind": "execute",
        "name": "sandbox-provenance-schema-version-shared-package",
        "title": "Land shared schema-version contract package with gct-pending-ai-provenance-hardening (Phase 5)",
        "description": "Per Decision 3 in the locked plan, the schema-version contract is meant to be a shared package between this initiative and `execute/gct-pending-ai-provenance-hardening` (currently on a different branch). Coordinate field names + schema-version constant location with that item before persisting `runOutcome` / `state` / `conversationId` / `costUsd` end-to-end. Until this lands, the wire-level fields added in Phases 1–2 are not persisted and readers see empty values.",
        "priority": 2,
        "effort": "M",
        "depends_on": ["execute/agent-manager-run-executor-apply-at-run-end-cutover"]
      },
      "rationale": "Plan's Phase 5 explicitly requires cross-initiative coordination; tracking it as its own item makes the dependency on the GCT branch visible."
    },
    {
      "id": "m6",
      "op": "add_item",
      "item": {
        "kind": "execute",
        "name": "agent-manager-spawn-surface-conversation-id-population",
        "title": "Populate Run.ConversationID / Run.ParentRunID at all spawn surfaces",
        "description": "Update web-console, swarm-manager queue, cron, and CLI spawn surfaces to populate `Run.ConversationID` and `Run.ParentRunID` directly, rather than relying on the inheritance fallback. Cross-cuts other repos. Also covers DB read-time normalization for legacy persisted runs that still carry `Acceptance.AutoApprove==true` / `RequiresApproval` (per the plan's Risks table).",
        "priority": 4,
        "effort": "M",
        "depends_on": ["execute/agent-manager-run-executor-apply-at-run-end-cutover"]
      },
      "rationale": "Execution agent flagged this as in-scope-but-deferred; the inheritance fallback covers the gap today, but the contract intent is for spawners to set these directly. Tracked as a follow-up so it doesn't get lost."
    },
    {
      "id": "m7",
      "op": "add_edge",
      "from": "execute/sandbox-runtime-e2e-verification",
      "to": "execute/agent-manager-run-executor-apply-at-run-end-cutover",
      "rationale": "E2E verification needs the actual behavior-flipping cut (Phase 3b), not just the seam — repoint the dependency to the load-bearing item."
    },
    {
      "id": "m8",
      "op": "add_edge",
      "from": "execute/agent-manager-default-sandboxing-rollout",
      "to": "execute/agent-manager-run-executor-apply-at-run-end-cutover",
      "rationale": "Rollout can't make sandboxing the default until Phase 3b actually flips behavior end-to-end."
    },
    {
      "id": "m9",
      "op": "add_edge",
      "from": "execute/agent-manager-default-sandboxing-rollout",
      "to": "execute/workspace-sandbox-manual-review-ttl-gc",
      "rationale": "Default rollout would otherwise leak manualReview sandboxes indefinitely; GC must be in place first."
    }
  ]
}
```

